  "title": "Ph Life Insurance Handbook — 3. Policy Lapse and Reinstatement Rules",
  "content": "## 3. Policy Lapse and Reinstatement Rules\n- **Lapse Condition**: If a premium is not settled within the 31-day grace period and there is insufficient cash value or automatic premium loan (APL) balance, the policy will lapse.\n- **Reinstatement Window**: Lapsed policies can be reinstated within three (3) years from the date of default.\n- **Reinstatement Requirements**:\n  1. Submission of Application for Reinstatement with Health Declaration.\n  2. Proof of insurability satisfactory to Darwix Underwriting.\n  3. Settlement of all overdue premiums with compound interest at 6% per annum.\n  4. Payment or reinstatement of any outstanding policy indebtedness.\n\n---",
